---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../lib/site.js';

const sections = [
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'Agreement' },
  { id: 'service', label: 'The service' },
  { id: 'accounts', label: 'Your account' },
  { id: 'trial', label: 'Free trial' },
  { id: 'plans', label: 'Plans and payment' },
  { id: 'use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'data', label: 'Your records' },
  { id: 'ip', label: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'availability', label: 'Availability' },
  { id: 'termination', label: 'Suspension and termination' },
  { id: 'disclaimers', label: 'Disclaimers' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to these terms' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The agreement between CashIko and the business using it: trial, plans, acceptable use, your records, disclaimers and governing law."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of service"
    lead={`The agreement between you and CashIko. Last updated ${LEGAL_UPDATED}.`}
  />

  <div class="shell grid gap-12 py-12 md:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr] md:gap-16 md:py-16">
    <nav class="md:sticky md:top-28 md:self-start" aria-label="Terms sections">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contents</p>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2">
        {sections.map((section, index) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`#${section.id}`} class="flex gap-2 text-[0.8125rem] text-forest-muted transition-colors hover:text-forest-dark">
              <span class="tabular text-[10px] text-warm">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              {section.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose-legal max-w-2xl">
      <section id="agreement">
        <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          By creating an account or using CashIko, you agree to these terms on behalf of the business you
          represent. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="service">
        <h2>2. The service</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko is a web-based record-keeping tool for small businesses. It records products, sales, utang,
          payments and expenses, and calculates stock levels and profit from the information you enter.
        </p>
        <p>
          CashIko is not an accounting firm, a tax adviser, or a BIR-accredited point-of-sale system. It does not
          issue official receipts, and it does not replace the records or receipts the law requires you to keep.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="accounts">
        <h2>3. Your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must provide accurate information and keep your login credentials secure.</li>
          <li>You are responsible for activity carried out under your account, including by staff you give access to.</li>
          <li>One account represents one business. Do not share an account between unrelated businesses.</li>
          <li>Tell us promptly if you believe your account has been accessed without permission.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="trial">
        <h2>4. Free trial</h2>
        <p>
          New accounts receive a fourteen-day trial of the full service without payment details. When the trial
          ends, access to paid features requires an active plan. We may change or end trial offers for new
          accounts at any time; changes do not apply retroactively to a trial already started.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="plans">
        <h2>5. Plans and payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Basic is ₱99 per month; Premium is ₱199 per month, in Philippine pesos.</li>
          <li>Fees are payable in advance for each billing period.</li>
          <li>You can change plans from Settings. Upgrades take effect immediately; downgrades take effect for the next period.</li>
          <li>Except where required by law, fees already paid are not refundable for a partial period.</li>
          <li>If a payment fails or a plan lapses, paid features may be suspended. Your records are not deleted immediately.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="use">
        <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use CashIko for unlawful purposes, including recording fictitious sales or concealing taxable income.</li>
          <li>Attempt to access another business’s records, or probe, scan or breach the service.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, resell, or provide the service to third parties as your own.</li>
          <li>Upload malicious files or content that infringes someone else’s rights.</li>
          <li>Use automated means to extract data beyond the export features we provide.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data">
        <h2>7. Your records</h2>
        <p>
          The data you enter belongs to you. You grant us the licence needed to store, process and display it so
          the service can function — nothing more. Our privacy policy explains what we collect and how it is
          handled.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the accuracy of what you record and for keeping your own copies of anything
          you are legally required to retain. Export your data before closing an account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="ip">
        <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko, its name, logo, interface and underlying code are owned by us or our licensors. These terms do
          not transfer any ownership to you. You may not use our marks without written permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="availability">
        <h2>9. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We work to keep CashIko available, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted service. Maintenance,
          provider outages and network conditions in your area can affect access. We may change, improve or
          retire features over time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="termination">
        <h2>10. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using CashIko at any time. We may suspend or terminate an account that violates these
          terms, poses a security risk, or is used unlawfully. Where practical, we will give notice and a chance
          to export your records first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="disclaimers">
        <h2>11. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko is provided “as is” and “as available”. The figures it shows depend entirely on the data you
          enter. We do not warrant that the service will be error-free, or that the reports it produces satisfy
          any particular accounting, tax or regulatory requirement. Decisions you make about your business remain
          yours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="liability">
        <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent allowed by Philippine law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental or
          consequential losses, or for lost profits or lost data arising from your use of the service. Where
          liability cannot be excluded, our total liability for any claim is limited to the fees you paid us in
          the three months before the event giving rise to the claim.
        </p>
        <p>Nothing in these terms limits rights that cannot be waived under Philippine law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="law">
        <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of the Philippines. Disputes will be brought
          before the proper courts of the Philippines, after a good-faith attempt to resolve the matter directly
          with us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms as the service evolves. The date at the top will change, and material changes
          will be communicated in the app or by email before they take effect. Continuing to use CashIko after a
          change means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
